# Walkthrough - Integrated OSB & SOA Enterprise Architecture

Oracle Service Bus (OSB 12c) proxy services, message pipelines, and business services have been added to [LendWise-Mortgage-System](file:///c:/ramu/Project_Assignment/RapidX/FreddeMac_Project_RapidX/Work/LendWise-Mortgage-System) alongside the existing Oracle SOA Suite BPEL Composites, forming a complete enterprise OSB + SOA combination layer in `lendwise-orchestration`.

## Changes Made

### 1. OSB Services Module Setup
Created the full [osb-services](file:///c:/ramu/Project_Assignment/RapidX/FreddeMac_Project_RapidX/Work/LendWise-Mortgage-System/lendwise-orchestration/osb-services) structure in `lendwise-orchestration` with parent build configuration in [osb-services/pom.xml](file:///c:/ramu/Project_Assignment/RapidX/FreddeMac_Project_RapidX/Work/LendWise-Mortgage-System/lendwise-orchestration/osb-services/pom.xml).

### 2. Maven Reactor Module Registration
Modified [lendwise-orchestration/pom.xml](file:///c:/ramu/Project_Assignment/RapidX/FreddeMac_Project_RapidX/Work/LendWise-Mortgage-System/lendwise-orchestration/pom.xml) to add `<module>osb-services</module>`.

```xml
    <modules>
        <module>java-adapters/dti-calculator</module>
